# Exceptions for script/offline_audit. One entry per line:
#
#   check | path glob | line regex (or *) | reason
#
# `check` is a check id: hosts, net-rust, net-cmd, net-string, net-git, net-bind, net-url,
# net-script, net-dep or binary-pin. The glob matches the repo-relative path (`*` also crosses `/`);
# for git dependencies the path is `git-dep:<package>/<path inside the package>`. The regex is
# matched case-insensitively against the matching line. Every entry needs a reason. An entry that
# matches nothing is reported, so remove entries when the code they cover is gone.
#
# Keep entries as narrow as the code they cover: one file and a regex for the reviewed construct,
# never a whole directory with `*`. A `binary-pin` entry pins a binary file: the glob is its exact
# path, the regex field its lowercase SHA-256, and the file is skipped by the hosts search while the
# hash is verified. `script/offline_audit --self-test` checks that the narrow entries still reject
# what they must.

# --- hosts (9.1) ---
hosts | CHANGES.md | * | describes the removals
hosts | script/offline_audit | * | holds the audit patterns
hosts | script/offline_audit.allowlist | * | documents the exceptions
hosts | deny.toml | * | allow-org for the build-time git forks, and the names of the banned crates
hosts | about.toml | * | comment naming the warpdotdev-hosted git sources that cargo-about skips (MASTER decision 15)
hosts | Cargo.lock | github\.com/warpdotdev/ | build-time git dependencies on the warpdotdev forks are kept (MASTER decision 15)
hosts | *Cargo.toml | github\.com/warpdotdev/ | build-time git dependencies on the warpdotdev forks are kept (MASTER decision 15)
hosts | crates/persistence/migrations/2022-07-29-164418_add_users/up.sql | firebase | historical migration, untouched (MASTER decision 14); DB-1 drops the table it creates
hosts | crates/persistence/migrations/2023-08-07-205653_add_user_profiles_table/up.sql | firebase | historical migration, untouched (MASTER decision 14); DB-1 drops the table it creates
hosts | crates/persistence/migrations/2026-09-29-000000_drop_dead_tables/down.sql | firebase | DB-1 down migration: recreates the dropped legacy tables, including their firebase_uid columns, to restore the old schema on rollback
hosts | crates/warpui_extras/src/secure_storage/linux.rs | releases\.warp\.dev/channel_versions\.json | secure-storage key material, not a network call; changing it would orphan stored secrets (MASTER decision 13)
binary-pin | app/assets/windows/x64/dxcompiler.dll | 75c019e3541980eea8ae661d81998d06f99627e3004c800532475a1c3551c6fb | third-party DirectX compiler binary (x64); `sEntry` matches `sentry` case-insensitively, so the file is pinned by hash instead of searched
binary-pin | app/assets/windows/arm64/dxcompiler.dll | e9803ca5a658fd87985d549bbaaeecd0feaed4c9b6490d688b0470ed3c7f9111 | third-party DirectX compiler binary (arm64); same reason
hosts | crates/secret_redaction/src/lib.rs | firebase | the redaction regex for leaked Firebase auth domains is a secret pattern, not a network call
hosts | crates/secret_redaction/src/lib.rs | platform\.openai\.com | doc comment naming where the format of an OpenAI API key is documented; the redaction patterns detect such keys, nothing fetches the page
hosts | crates/secret_redaction/src/lib_tests.rs | firebase | tests of that redaction regex
hosts | crates/secret_redaction/src/lib_tests.rs | AIza | fake Google API key that the redaction tests must detect
hosts | crates/warp_completer/src/signatures/legacy/generator_policy/denied.rs | "firebase" | the denied completion generator of the `firebase` CLI spec: a spec name, not a host
hosts | crates/warp_completer/src/signatures/legacy/generator_policy_tests.rs | \|firebase\| | regex in the completion-generator policy test that names the `firebase` CLI as a network tool
hosts | crates/lsp/src/config_tests.rs | firebase | path of an npm package (`node_modules/@firebase/auth`) used as a URI fixture
hosts | crates/persistence/test_data/pre_drop_dead_tables_seed.sql | firebase | seeds the columns of the pre-DB-1 schema that the migration drops
hosts | crates/integration/tests/data/test_json_object.sqlite | firebase_uid | legacy cloud-object fixture: its pre-DB-1 schema (users.firebase_uid) is dropped by the startup migration
hosts | crates/warp_core/src/paths.rs | /opt/warpdotdev | example install path in a doc comment (MASTER decision 17)
hosts | flake.nix | /opt/warpdotdev | install paths stay unchanged (MASTER decision 17)
hosts | resources/linux/* | opt/warpdotdev|%\{prefix\}/warpdotdev | install paths stay unchanged (MASTER decision 17); any other warpdotdev mention here is a finding
hosts | script/linux/* | opt/warpdotdev | install paths stay unchanged (MASTER decision 17); any other warpdotdev mention here is a finding
hosts | script/windows/windows-installer.iss | Warp\.dev | registry base stays unchanged (MASTER decision 17)
hosts | crates/warpui_extras/src/user_preferences/registry_backed.rs | Warp\.dev | registry base stays unchanged (MASTER decision 17)

# --- network-capable Rust (9.2) ---
net-rust | crates/http_client/src/lib.rs | ^\s*use reqwest::IntoUrl;$ | the shared HTTP client wraps reqwest; its only consumers are node_runtime and the language server installer (deny.toml wrappers)
net-rust | crates/http_client/src/lib.rs | reqwest::(Client|ClientBuilder|RequestBuilder|Request|Response|Result|Error|Body|Url)\b(?!::) | the wrapper's own types; a call such as `reqwest::Client::new()` or `reqwest::get` does not match
net-rust | crates/http_client/src/lib.rs | reqwest::Client::builder\(\) | the wrapper builds its client here
net-rust | crates/node_runtime/src/lib.rs | ^\s*client: http_client::Client(::new\(\))?,$ | Node download for lsp only, through the http_client wrapper
net-rust | crates/node_runtime/src/lib.rs | -> &http_client::Client \{ | accessor of that client
net-rust | crates/local_control/src/client.rs | ^\s*use std::net::Shutdown;$ | the warpctrl client shuts down its loopback stream
net-rust | crates/local_control/src/client.rs | reqwest::blocking::Client::new\(\) | the warpctrl client; discovery accepts only 127.0.0.1 endpoints (discovery.rs)
net-rust | app/src/local_control/mod.rs | ^\s*use axum::(body::Bytes|extract::State|http::header::\{AUTHORIZATION, HOST, ORIGIN\}|http::\{HeaderMap, StatusCode\}|response::\{IntoResponse, Response\}|routing::post|\{Json, Router\});$ | axum types of the loopback warpctrl server
net-rust | app/src/local_control/mod.rs | tokio::net::TcpListener::bind\(SocketAddr::from\(\( | the warpctrl listener; the bind check requires a 127.0.0.1 address next to it
net-rust | app/src/local_control/mod.rs | axum::serve\(listener, router\) | serves the warpctrl router on that listener
net-rust | app/src/local_control/mod.rs | tokio::net::Unix(Listener|Stream) | Unix-socket credential broker for warpctrl
net-rust | app/src/local_control/mod_tests.rs | ^\s*use axum::(body::Bytes|extract::State|http::header::\{AUTHORIZATION, HOST, ORIGIN\}|http::\{HeaderMap, HeaderValue\}); | axum types in the warpctrl server tests
net-rust | app/src/local_control/mod_tests.rs | tokio::net::UnixStream::pair\(\)|axum::http::StatusCode | in-process socket pair and status codes in the warpctrl server tests
net-rust | crates/warp_completer/src/signatures/legacy/generator_policy/allowed.rs | "hyper" | the allowed `hyper list` completion generator (the Hyper terminal's plugin lister), not the hyper crate
net-rust | * | ^\s*(pub )?use std::net::\{?((IpAddr|Ipv4Addr|Ipv6Addr|SocketAddr)(, )?)+\}?; | address types only, no sockets
net-rust | app/src/terminal/model/session/command_executor/offline_environment_tests.rs | ^\s*use std::net::\{TcpListener, TcpStream\};$ | loopback canary HTTP server of the offline-environment tests (stands in for the internet; binds 127.0.0.1 only)
net-rust | app/src/terminal/model/session/command_executor/offline_environment_tests.rs | address: std::net::SocketAddr, | address of that canary
net-rust | app/src/terminal/model/session/command_executor/offline_environment_tests.rs | TcpListener::bind\("127\.0\.0\.1:0"\) | the canary listener, loopback only
net-rust | app/src/terminal/model/session/command_executor/offline_environment_tests.rs | fn serve\(mut stream: TcpStream | the canary's per-connection handler

# --- subprocesses that can reach a network (9.2) ---
net-cmd | app/src/util/git.rs | Command::new\("git"\) | local git for the code-review panel and the commit dialog (MASTER decision 20)
net-cmd | app/src/util/git.rs | Command::new\("gh"\) | the only `gh` in the app: `gh repo view`, `gh pr view` and `gh pr create`, checked by the gh command check of the audit (MASTER decisions 20, 22)
net-cmd | app/src/search/files/model.rs | Command::new\("git"\) | `git status --porcelain` for changed files
net-cmd | crates/warp_util/src/git.rs | Command::new\("git"\) | `run_git_command`: local git; remote verbs are rejected by the net-git check
net-cmd | app/src/util/git_tests.rs | Command::new\("git"\) | test repository setup
net-cmd | app/src/terminal/model/session/command_executor/offline_environment_tests.rs | Command::new\("git"\) | test repository setup for the offline-environment tests
net-cmd | crates/integration/src/test/code_review.rs | Command::new\("git"\) | integration test repository setup
net-cmd | app/src/terminal/model/session/command_executor/remote_command_executor.rs | Command::new\("ssh"\) | the user's own SSH session (ControlMaster command executor)

# --- command strings (9.2) ---
net-string | app/src/terminal/ssh/util.rs | String::from\("sftp "\) | `sftp` command line of the user's own SSH session
net-string | app/src/terminal/view/ssh_file_upload.rs | String::from\("sftp "\) | SSH drag-and-drop upload over the user's own SSH session
net-string | app/src/settings_view/warpify_page.rs | "ssh subshell warpify session" | label text, not a command

# --- remote git operations (9.2) ---
net-git | app/src/util/git.rs | "push" | `git push` from the commit and push dialog, an explicit user action (MASTER decision 20)

# --- URLs in the crates that fetch (9.2) ---
net-url | crates/lsp/src/install.rs | const GITHUB_API_URL: &str = "https://api.github.com"; | release lookup of the opt-in language server downloads
net-url | crates/node_runtime/src/lib.rs | format!\("https://nodejs.org/dist/ | Node.js download of the opt-in language server downloads
net-url | crates/node_runtime/src/lib.rs | format!\("https://registry.npmjs.org/ | npm package lookup of the opt-in language server downloads

# --- sockets bound to every interface (9.2) ---
net-bind | crates/secret_redaction/src/lib_tests.rs | let double_colon = "::"; | a string used by a redaction test, not an address

# --- git dependencies (9.2) ---
# The audit skips `src/generated_workflows/` of warp-workflows (written by its build script from
# committed YAML specs; absent in an unbuilt checkout), so nothing here may depend on it.
# Completion generators of warp-command-signatures: shell commands the completion engine could run.
# Each network one is denied by generator_policy/denied.rs, so these lines are inert. A new hit is
# a new generator: classify it there first (the audit also fails on unclassified generator names).
net-dep | git-dep:warp-command-signatures/src/generators/deno.rs | cdn\.deno\.land/deno/meta/versions\.json | denied generator deno/deno_versions
net-dep | git-dep:warp-command-signatures/src/generators/deployctl.rs | cdn\.deno\.land/deploy/meta/versions\.json | denied generator deployctl/deploy_versions
net-dep | git-dep:warp-command-signatures/src/generators/elm.rs | package\.elm-lang\.org/search\.json | denied generator elm/elm_packages
net-dep | git-dep:warp-command-signatures/src/generators/fig_teams.rs | npx -y fig-teams@latest | denied generators fig-teams@latest/teams_list and users_for_selected_team
net-dep | git-dep:warp-command-signatures/src/generators/fig_token.rs | curl -sfL 'https://crates\.io/api/v1/crates | denied generator cargo/crates_io_search
net-dep | git-dep:warp-command-signatures/src/generators/fig_token.rs | curl -sL 'https://api\.github\.com/users/ | denied generator degit/github_user_repos
net-dep | git-dep:warp-command-signatures/src/generators/fig_token.rs | curl -s -H 'Accept: application/json' 'https://api\.npms\.io/v2/search | denied npms_search generators of bun, expo, expo-cli, ni, npm, pnpm, rush and yarn
net-dep | git-dep:warp-command-signatures/src/generators/gh.rs | gh api graphql | denied generator gh/api_graphql_string_viewer
net-dep | git-dep:warp-command-signatures/src/generators/hyper.rs | hyper | the allowed `hyper list` generator (the Hyper terminal's plugin lister), not the hyper crate
net-dep | git-dep:warp-command-signatures/src/generators/mod.rs | mod hyper;|hyper::generator\(\) | registration of that generator
net-dep | git-dep:warp-command-signatures/src/generators/npm.rs | curl -sf 'https://registry\.npmjs\.org/-/v1/search | denied generator npm/npm_registry_search
net-dep | git-dep:warp-command-signatures/src/generators/ns.rs | curl -sfL .* https://api\.github\.com/repos/NativeScript/ | denied generators nativescript, ns and tns / nativescript_templates
net-dep | git-dep:warp-command-signatures/src/generators/scp.rs | "ssh\{\} -o BatchMode=yes | denied generator scp/remote_paths
net-dep | git-dep:warp-command-signatures/src/generators/sdk.rs | curl -s https://api\.sdkman\.io/ | denied generator sdk/available_versions
net-dep | git-dep:warp-command-signatures/src/generators/stepzen.rs | curl https://api\.github\.com/repos/steprz/ | denied generator stepzen/github_schemas
net-dep | git-dep:warp-command-signatures/src/generators/asdf.rs | github\.com/asdf-vm/asdf-nodejs\.git | unit-test fixture string inside the dependency
net-dep | git-dep:warp-command-signatures/src/generators/vagrant.rs | "http://example\.com/box" | unit-test fixture string inside the dependency

# --- developer and CI bootstrap (9.2) ---
# These fetch third-party toolchains for building the app; nothing here ships in the app.
net-script | script/install_cargo_binstall | * | fetches cargo-binstall from GitHub releases at build time
net-script | script/install_rust | * | rustup installer
net-script | script/linux/configure_musl_toolchain | * | musl toolchain download at build time
net-script | script/linux/install_build_deps | * | protoc download at build time
net-script | script/linux/install_linuxdeploy | * | AppImage tooling download at build time
net-script | script/macos/bootstrap | * | Homebrew and rustup installers
net-script | script/windows/bootstrap.ps1 | * | rustup installer
net-script | docker/linux-dev/Dockerfile | * | developer container image: installs curl, the GitHub CLI apt key and rustup while the image is built; never shipped in the app
net-script | script/offline_audit | * | holds the audit patterns
net-script | script/offline_audit.allowlist | * | documents the exceptions
